WEBVTT

00:00:09.500 --> 00:00:10.590
Now that the rainy season has started,

00:00:11.060 --> 00:00:12.550
it rains quite a lot.

00:00:13.830 --> 00:00:15.250
I don't like the rainy season.

00:00:15.980 --> 00:00:20.170
As the humidity rises, so does my misery.

00:00:23.870 --> 00:00:25.530
I'm Chizuru Tachibana.

00:00:25.530 --> 00:00:28.000
My best feature is 
 the mole under my eye.

00:00:28.620 --> 00:00:29.800
I'm Yuta Asaba.

00:00:30.290 --> 00:00:31.840
I have a younger twin brother.

00:00:32.200 --> 00:00:33.650
You're identical.

00:00:36.150 --> 00:00:37.830
I'm Shun Matsuoka.

00:00:38.240 --> 00:00:40.970
Let's see... I'm in the tea club.

00:00:41.320 --> 00:00:44.100
Shun-chan, you're so cute.

00:00:44.100 --> 00:00:45.190
What?

00:00:45.770 --> 00:00:47.380
I'm Masaki Sato.

00:00:47.840 --> 00:00:48.940
I'm a first year.

00:00:49.190 --> 00:00:51.470
Finally, a girl.

00:00:51.920 --> 00:00:54.160
Don't tell me you're a boy, too.

00:00:55.500 --> 00:00:58.700
Yuki Asaba. 
 My favorite doujin is Anime-ja.

00:00:59.000 --> 00:01:01.700
Yeah! It's cool!

00:01:04.330 --> 00:01:06.430
Time for the final introduction.

00:01:06.770 --> 00:01:08.880
The floor is yours!

00:01:10.660 --> 00:01:13.710
Hey, Kanamecchi. Don't stop the flow.

00:01:13.980 --> 00:01:16.920
You've got to introduce yourself at a mixer.

00:01:20.850 --> 00:01:22.090
And recently,

00:01:22.570 --> 00:01:27.270
more things that contribute to my
 misery have sprung up around me.

00:03:00.070 --> 00:03:02.410
Come on, hurry. Come on.

00:03:02.800 --> 00:03:04.900
Why a mixer?

00:03:05.200 --> 00:03:08.040
I'm only here because you insisted I come.

00:03:08.890 --> 00:03:11.120
You're no fun.

00:03:11.410 --> 00:03:13.400
I even had Yukki and Shun-chan...

00:03:13.400 --> 00:03:16.960
pretend to be girls to even up the numbers.

00:03:17.500 --> 00:03:20.010
I don't understand why you did that.

00:03:20.980 --> 00:03:22.970
Forget about this shy boy.

00:03:22.970 --> 00:03:27.310
Okay. What kind of guy do you like?

00:03:28.200 --> 00:03:29.180
How about it, Yukki?

00:03:31.060 --> 00:03:32.500
Let's see...

00:03:33.030 --> 00:03:36.730
I suppose someone who could prove to me...

00:03:36.730 --> 00:03:38.940
that there are things more
 important than money.

00:03:39.170 --> 00:03:41.680
I'll do it! I'll prove it to you!

00:03:41.680 --> 00:03:45.170
I'll even embrace your entire past.

00:03:45.170 --> 00:03:47.450
I promise I'll do it.

00:03:49.690 --> 00:03:50.850
What about you, Shun-san?

00:03:52.240 --> 00:03:55.370
U-Um, someone kind, I guess.

00:03:55.370 --> 00:03:59.530
You'll fall in love with someone as long as they're nice?

00:04:01.520 --> 00:04:04.470
Hey, Kanamecchi, what's your type?

00:04:04.710 --> 00:04:05.970
I dunno.

00:04:07.480 --> 00:04:09.720
This guy's into older women.

00:04:10.830 --> 00:04:12.920
Much older women.

00:04:12.920 --> 00:04:15.020
No way! You like mature women?

00:04:15.360 --> 00:04:16.520
No.

00:04:16.740 --> 00:04:20.690
Yuki-Mama, Kanamecchi's trying to hurt me.

00:04:21.070 --> 00:04:24.180
All men are like that.

00:04:24.180 --> 00:04:26.490
They never show any kindness.

00:04:27.870 --> 00:04:29.320
Yuki-Mama.

00:04:29.320 --> 00:04:31.300
What are you guys doing?

00:04:31.300 --> 00:04:33.580
And why are we having this mixer?

00:04:33.940 --> 00:04:37.080
Youth is all about mixers.

00:04:37.420 --> 00:04:38.340
What?

00:04:38.710 --> 00:04:42.340
Young people must never forget about mixers.

00:04:43.100 --> 00:04:46.840
But you've forgotten that 
this group isn't mixer material.

00:04:47.090 --> 00:04:48.470
Not to mention the weather.

00:04:49.400 --> 00:04:50.460
The weather?

00:04:51.500 --> 00:04:52.280
Huh?

00:04:53.480 --> 00:04:54.980
Uh oh.

00:04:55.460 --> 00:04:57.980
You monkey!

00:05:02.140 --> 00:05:05.010
Damn that monkey.

00:05:08.790 --> 00:05:10.800
Oh, Tsukahara-kun.

00:05:10.800 --> 00:05:13.450
I'm done here. It's all yours.

00:05:17.460 --> 00:05:20.760
I'm impressed you're partying outside in this weather.

00:05:20.760 --> 00:05:22.590
There's nothing impressive about it.

00:05:23.210 --> 00:05:24.590
Aside from Tachibana-kun,

00:05:24.590 --> 00:05:26.550
you're all childhood friends, aren't you?

00:05:26.550 --> 00:05:30.010
Yes, since kindergarten.

00:05:30.010 --> 00:05:31.450
I see.

00:05:31.450 --> 00:05:35.240
I'm sure you've all changed a lot since then.

00:05:35.240 --> 00:05:36.770
We haven't changed one bit.

00:05:37.170 --> 00:05:39.940
Shun's always been a flowery guy,

00:05:39.940 --> 00:05:42.600
and Yuta and Yuki were even 
more problematic as little kids.

00:05:42.600 --> 00:05:44.350
A couple of precocious preschoolers.

00:05:46.740 --> 00:05:48.940
You're right.

00:05:48.940 --> 00:05:53.210
Children are always more precocious than adults think.

00:05:53.980 --> 00:05:57.910
While I was working in high school, 
I visited a kindergarten,

00:05:57.910 --> 00:05:59.510
and the children there were a handful.

00:06:00.680 --> 00:06:04.590
<i>Now you mention it, I guess I was pretty precocious, too.</i>

00:06:07.130 --> 00:06:08.970
Kaori-sensei.

00:06:08.970 --> 00:06:09.590
Yes, yes.

00:06:09.820 --> 00:06:12.100
Kaname-kun, what's wrong?

00:06:13.440 --> 00:06:15.560
I've figured it out.

00:06:16.090 --> 00:06:18.660
No matter how much it snows,

00:06:18.660 --> 00:06:22.060
the flowers of love will always bloom.

00:06:22.800 --> 00:06:25.250
Kaname-kun, you reek of cheesiness.

00:06:25.250 --> 00:06:26.780
That's not what that means.

00:06:29.810 --> 00:06:34.520
The students from Homare High School are here to help us work.

00:06:34.520 --> 00:06:38.140
They'll be your teachers for the day.

00:06:38.140 --> 00:06:41.410
This is Koichi-sensei and Akira-sensei.

00:06:41.410 --> 00:06:42.560
Nice to meet you.

00:06:42.560 --> 00:06:43.920
Nice to meet you!

00:06:48.400 --> 00:06:51.210
Um, what should we do?

00:06:51.210 --> 00:06:54.300
You can start by reading them picture books.

00:06:54.620 --> 00:06:57.200
<i>Who does he think he is,</i>

00:06:57.200 --> 00:07:00.130
<i>talking to my Kaori-sensei like that?</i>

00:07:00.510 --> 00:07:02.100
Love is fleeting.

00:07:02.100 --> 00:07:03.560
It's not over yet.

00:07:04.420 --> 00:07:07.530
<i>I'll never lose to a guy like that.</i>

00:07:11.160 --> 00:07:13.050
This brings back memories.

00:07:13.340 --> 00:07:18.430
When I was your age, I cried when I read this.

00:07:18.430 --> 00:07:20.540
I felt so bad for Snow White.

00:07:20.540 --> 00:07:22.160
Did you really?

00:07:22.160 --> 00:07:24.080
Yeah. I was a cry baby.

00:07:25.140 --> 00:07:26.620
How lame.

00:07:26.620 --> 00:07:29.120
How's can you protect the 
princess when you are crying.

00:07:29.120 --> 00:07:32.550
I'd fight the witch before anything happened to her.

00:07:32.780 --> 00:07:33.980
I'm sorry.

00:07:33.980 --> 00:07:37.370
He believes he can solve any problem with money.

00:07:37.370 --> 00:07:38.700
No, with strength.

00:07:38.880 --> 00:07:41.080
Look, look.

00:07:41.080 --> 00:07:43.180
Look at mine first.

00:07:43.180 --> 00:07:44.640
Yours is terrible.

00:07:43.180 --> 00:07:44.760
Oh, um...

00:07:44.640 --> 00:07:46.570
No, yours is.

00:07:45.240 --> 00:07:46.570
Don't fight...

00:07:47.220 --> 00:07:49.670
Your rival's popular.

00:07:51.620 --> 00:07:56.220
He thinks he's so great because 
 he's sorta so tall and good looking.

00:07:56.940 --> 00:07:58.640
I'm way better.

00:07:58.640 --> 00:08:01.490
Yeah. Compared to your good looks,

00:08:01.490 --> 00:08:04.800
his good looks don't seem inferior at all.

00:08:05.710 --> 00:08:07.910
That means I'm worse than him.

00:08:07.910 --> 00:08:09.990
It's okay, Kaname-kun.

00:08:09.990 --> 00:08:12.460
There are always obstacles to love.

00:08:12.460 --> 00:08:15.340
They say your first love never works out.

00:08:15.340 --> 00:08:17.100
That's not helping!

00:08:22.190 --> 00:08:24.060
Hooray! A snowball fight!

00:08:28.610 --> 00:08:30.020
Now you've done it.

00:08:30.020 --> 00:08:30.800
Get back here!

00:08:38.690 --> 00:08:40.170
Are you okay by yourself?

00:08:43.250 --> 00:08:45.510
Does he...

00:08:45.830 --> 00:08:47.110
He hates you.

00:08:48.090 --> 00:08:50.460
He does.

00:08:50.930 --> 00:08:52.250
<i>It's okay.</i>

00:08:52.250 --> 00:08:55.680
<i>I love Kaori-sensei.</i>

00:08:59.000 --> 00:09:01.600
Kaname-kun, that's huge.

00:09:03.520 --> 00:09:08.290
Why don't we combine yours with 
mine and make a snowman?

00:09:11.440 --> 00:09:13.860
I'll stack them.

00:09:20.930 --> 00:09:21.790
Kaori-se—

00:09:23.250 --> 00:09:24.470
Are you all right?

00:09:32.590 --> 00:09:34.110
S-Sorry.

00:09:34.110 --> 00:09:35.010
Don't worry about it.

00:09:41.080 --> 00:09:42.370
There you go.

00:09:42.770 --> 00:09:44.920
Your snowman's complete.

00:09:48.600 --> 00:09:49.980
Are you okay?

00:09:52.710 --> 00:09:55.260
I don't need your pity.

00:09:55.260 --> 00:09:56.150
Jerk!

00:10:12.960 --> 00:10:16.260
Um, did I do something?

00:10:16.670 --> 00:10:18.430
Don't get the wrong idea.

00:10:20.560 --> 00:10:24.120
I could've helped Kaori-sensei, too.

00:10:27.530 --> 00:10:30.720
<i>What? What is this?</i>

00:10:31.540 --> 00:10:32.890
<i>I look like such an idiot.</i>

00:10:33.490 --> 00:10:34.890
You're a cool little guy.

00:10:38.530 --> 00:10:40.530
<b>"Snow White"</b>

00:10:41.550 --> 00:10:47.190
I was just crying, but you're different.

00:10:47.190 --> 00:10:49.560
You're there to fight for her and defend her.

00:10:50.500 --> 00:10:51.580
You're a cool little guy.

00:10:57.520 --> 00:10:58.670
<i>Dammit.</i>

00:10:59.680 --> 00:11:00.900
<i>I hope...</i>

00:11:01.410 --> 00:11:02.850
<i>Someday, I hope...</i>

00:11:05.940 --> 00:11:07.960
<i>I can be just like him.</i>

00:11:10.750 --> 00:11:12.240
<i>How embarrassing.</i>

00:11:12.750 --> 00:11:15.820
<i>I know I was just a kid, but...</i>

00:11:15.820 --> 00:11:18.750
<i>Dammit, my face is burning.</i>

00:11:19.060 --> 00:11:19.830
Huh?

00:11:20.380 --> 00:11:21.810
Is something wrong?

00:11:21.810 --> 00:11:24.000
No, it's nothing.

00:11:24.430 --> 00:11:25.910
If you'll excuse me...

00:11:36.520 --> 00:11:40.470
<i>I wonder how those kids are doing.</i>

00:11:58.510 --> 00:12:00.620
Damn.

00:12:00.620 --> 00:12:02.020
It's that stupid monkey's fault...

00:12:02.020 --> 00:12:05.450
for making us do that pointless mixer.

00:12:11.530 --> 00:12:13.150
It's really chucking it down.

00:12:19.070 --> 00:12:20.920
He's a surprisingly deep sleeper.

00:12:21.980 --> 00:12:24.000
He's defenseless.

00:12:24.000 --> 00:12:27.360
You shouldn't do that.

00:12:27.360 --> 00:12:28.750
Now, now.

00:12:35.910 --> 00:12:38.400
Oh. Kaname, you're looking well.

00:12:39.290 --> 00:12:40.650
What are you doing here?

00:12:40.650 --> 00:12:43.130
We came to visit.

00:12:43.130 --> 00:12:44.370
Visit?

00:12:45.740 --> 00:12:49.090
I can't believe you caught a cold
 as soon as the season changed.

00:12:49.090 --> 00:12:51.060
Kanamecchi, you're like an old man.

00:12:51.060 --> 00:12:52.870
Whose fault is it I caught this cold?

00:12:52.870 --> 00:12:55.020
Ow. You're mean.

00:12:55.020 --> 00:12:57.820
And we came all the way here to visit you, old man.

00:12:57.820 --> 00:12:59.370
Who are you calling "old man"?

00:12:59.370 --> 00:13:01.860
Kaname-kun, are you okay?

00:13:01.860 --> 00:13:03.920
I'm fine.

00:13:10.440 --> 00:13:11.970
Yuki!

00:13:11.970 --> 00:13:14.040
Why are you taking pictures of me?

00:13:14.040 --> 00:13:15.000
Delete that!

00:13:15.000 --> 00:13:16.230
Come on, give me your phone!

00:13:16.450 --> 00:13:17.940
Give you my phone?

00:13:18.280 --> 00:13:20.860
My phone with all sorts of personal information on it?

00:13:21.090 --> 00:13:22.110
What?

00:13:22.470 --> 00:13:25.320
The personal information 
of the top student in the grade...

00:13:25.320 --> 00:13:26.410
doesn't come cheap.

00:13:29.630 --> 00:13:30.830
That's nothing like him.

00:13:30.830 --> 00:13:33.700
It's nothing like him, but I like 
your Kanamecchi impression.

00:13:33.700 --> 00:13:35.340
What's good about it?

00:13:35.340 --> 00:13:38.130
Don't you dare laugh, too.

00:13:39.240 --> 00:13:40.630
Sorry.

00:13:41.050 --> 00:13:42.470
Enough.

00:13:42.470 --> 00:13:43.790
I'll force you to...

00:13:43.790 --> 00:13:46.130
Don't, Kaname-kun. You have to rest.

00:13:46.130 --> 00:13:47.250
Let go, Shun.

00:13:47.250 --> 00:13:50.140
I can't rest peacefully as long as they're here.

00:13:50.500 --> 00:13:52.360
Hey, do these look good on me?

00:13:52.610 --> 00:13:56.460
Yeah, but if you wear them too long, 
you'll damage your eyes.

00:13:58.350 --> 00:14:02.340
Your house sure is nice, Kanamecchi.

00:14:15.390 --> 00:14:18.900
Thank you for coming to visit Kaname-kun.

00:14:19.260 --> 00:14:20.980
Oh, thank you.

00:14:21.880 --> 00:14:24.630
I haven't seen you before.

00:14:24.850 --> 00:14:27.420
Nice to meet you. I am Kaname-kun's mother.

00:14:28.780 --> 00:14:30.550
I'm Chizuru Tachibana.

00:14:31.020 --> 00:14:34.840
You're quite young. And beautiful.

00:14:34.840 --> 00:14:36.810
Why, thank you.

00:14:37.340 --> 00:14:40.470
Kaname-kun, he just made a pass at me.

00:14:40.470 --> 00:14:41.560
Are you jealous?

00:14:41.920 --> 00:14:43.070
Not really.

00:14:43.280 --> 00:14:45.420
Hey, you shouldn't make a woman cry.

00:14:45.420 --> 00:14:46.820
Why is she crying anyway?

00:14:50.990 --> 00:14:54.080
Huh? There's one extra juice.

00:14:54.590 --> 00:14:56.230
Oh, that's mine.

00:14:56.230 --> 00:14:57.830
You're gonna drink in here, too?

00:14:58.100 --> 00:15:02.800
Because I want to talk to you, Kaname-kun.

00:15:02.800 --> 00:15:04.340
You can talk to me any time.

00:15:04.560 --> 00:15:07.420
Liar. You're always so brusque.

00:15:07.420 --> 00:15:09.930
You've even stopped holding my hand recently.

00:15:10.600 --> 00:15:13.160
I haven't held your hand in years.

00:15:13.160 --> 00:15:14.930
I wouldn't call that recent.

00:15:15.660 --> 00:15:17.770
Am I that annoying?

00:15:18.170 --> 00:15:20.690
Am I really that annoying?

00:15:21.600 --> 00:15:23.370
What are you saying?

00:15:23.960 --> 00:15:27.350
That's not it. It's just how it goes.

00:15:27.350 --> 00:15:31.700
But you said... but you said you loved me.

00:15:34.900 --> 00:15:38.350
Can't we go back to the way we used to be?

00:15:38.350 --> 00:15:40.430
Is it too late?

00:15:40.430 --> 00:15:41.300
Hey.

00:15:41.300 --> 00:15:43.170
Has the love disappeared?

00:15:43.390 --> 00:15:46.270
That's not something you should say to your son.

00:15:47.400 --> 00:15:49.110
You have to remember the day...

00:15:49.110 --> 00:15:52.500
you told her she'd be your first and last.

00:15:52.500 --> 00:15:54.990
That never happened! We're family!

00:15:56.810 --> 00:15:58.810
I need to go to the supermarket.

00:16:06.840 --> 00:16:08.480
Oh, Hisa-chan.

00:16:08.480 --> 00:16:10.550
Oh, hello.

00:16:10.550 --> 00:16:11.350
Hello.

00:16:11.350 --> 00:16:13.990
Your mom's pretty cute, Kanamecchi.

00:16:15.660 --> 00:16:18.710
I try to avoid introducing her to my friends.

00:16:19.180 --> 00:16:22.000
Kaname-kun, you should lie down.

00:16:22.000 --> 00:16:23.360
I'm fine.

00:16:24.130 --> 00:16:26.710
Oh, right. Will you be able to make up...

00:16:26.710 --> 00:16:28.010
for the classes you missed today?

00:16:28.010 --> 00:16:29.720
I had Yuki-kun and Chizuru-kun take notes for—

00:16:29.680 --> 00:16:33.010
I'll be fine. I'm sure they didn't take notes anyway.

00:16:33.230 --> 00:16:34.460
Then, I'll...

00:16:34.460 --> 00:16:36.040
I said I'll be fine.

00:16:40.810 --> 00:16:43.480
I see. You're right.

00:16:44.390 --> 00:16:47.570
I just have to memorize the stuff...

00:16:47.570 --> 00:16:49.970
we're doing right now, so it'll be fine.

00:16:50.810 --> 00:16:52.490
Kaname.

00:16:53.150 --> 00:16:55.420
I heard you caught a cold.

00:16:55.420 --> 00:16:56.620
Hisako-chan.

00:16:56.900 --> 00:16:58.620
Shun-kun, it's good to see you again.

00:17:00.060 --> 00:17:02.290
You grew your hair out again.

00:17:02.290 --> 00:17:04.990
A girl barged into Kanamecchi's room!

00:17:04.990 --> 00:17:06.350
Who is she? Is she your girlfriend?

00:17:06.350 --> 00:17:08.600
How naughty!

00:17:08.600 --> 00:17:10.780
Stop saying nasty stuff.

00:17:10.780 --> 00:17:12.730
She's just a childhood friend.

00:17:12.730 --> 00:17:14.840
Who'd date this brute?

00:17:18.240 --> 00:17:21.310
Nice to meet you. I'm Hisako Aida.

00:17:21.310 --> 00:17:23.980
Nice to meet you. I'm Chizuru Tachibana.

00:17:25.010 --> 00:17:27.640
Ow. You shouldn't punch the sick.

00:17:27.640 --> 00:17:30.940
You should shut up and rest like a sick person.

00:17:33.450 --> 00:17:34.700
What's this?

00:17:35.050 --> 00:17:38.440
I found a photo in your desk drawer.

00:17:39.590 --> 00:17:41.700
Hey, don't touch my desk!

00:17:42.680 --> 00:17:44.060
Let me see.

00:17:44.060 --> 00:17:45.940
What do we have here?

00:17:46.740 --> 00:17:47.460
Hey!

00:17:48.900 --> 00:17:52.780
Isn't this from that time your family and mine...

00:17:52.780 --> 00:17:55.470
had that... think it was a barbecue?

00:17:55.730 --> 00:17:56.880
Is it really?

00:17:56.880 --> 00:17:58.120
That's all?

00:17:58.120 --> 00:18:01.110
I was hoping for something more unexpected.

00:18:02.360 --> 00:18:07.480
You don't have anything but study material on your desk.

00:18:07.700 --> 00:18:10.730
Your disappointment's making me angry.

00:18:10.730 --> 00:18:12.240
Who's this?

00:18:12.240 --> 00:18:15.120
That's my sister. Her name's Shizuna.

00:18:16.380 --> 00:18:17.700
Enough already.

00:18:20.240 --> 00:18:24.690
I still can't believe you'd treasure a photo like that.

00:18:24.690 --> 00:18:26.270
That's not it.

00:18:26.270 --> 00:18:27.650
I stuck it in there because...

00:18:27.650 --> 00:18:29.450
I didn't have anywhere else to keep it.

00:18:29.450 --> 00:18:30.250
Really?

00:18:30.250 --> 00:18:33.000
Shut up. Go away.

00:18:39.850 --> 00:18:44.440
If you try anything weird, I'll throw you out.

00:18:48.470 --> 00:18:51.310
I could've done it myself.

00:18:51.800 --> 00:18:54.120
Shun-kun, you're a guest.

00:18:54.120 --> 00:18:56.630
So are you, Hisako-chan.

00:18:57.630 --> 00:19:00.780
I've spent lots of time here since I was little.

00:19:01.620 --> 00:19:03.330
And now, after all these years...

00:19:03.770 --> 00:19:05.090
Oh, his medicine.

00:19:05.490 --> 00:19:08.360
Did Kaname-kun take any this afternoon?

00:19:08.360 --> 00:19:09.960
Should we take it to him?

00:19:10.250 --> 00:19:12.840
You worry too much.

00:19:14.510 --> 00:19:15.960
Kaname-kun...

00:19:18.040 --> 00:19:21.970
He's never relied on others.

00:19:22.590 --> 00:19:25.720
He's always helping me with things,

00:19:26.050 --> 00:19:29.560
but I never get to help him.

00:19:29.790 --> 00:19:32.600
Oh, right.

00:19:33.200 --> 00:19:34.420
Yeah.

00:19:34.920 --> 00:19:36.320
Well, that's fine, isn't it?

00:19:36.680 --> 00:19:37.570
Huh?

00:19:38.070 --> 00:19:39.740
You think so?

00:19:40.660 --> 00:19:42.740
I'm sure he doesn't mind.

00:19:44.580 --> 00:19:48.490
Chizuru's Ultra Dive.

00:19:49.740 --> 00:19:52.790
A perfect score! He's done it!

00:19:52.790 --> 00:19:54.790
He's set a new world record!

00:19:52.790 --> 00:19:54.790
You scored a zero!

00:19:54.790 --> 00:19:57.500
That hurts. Get off, you monkey.

00:19:58.130 --> 00:20:00.970
What's all that noise?

00:20:03.260 --> 00:20:06.330
Chizuru-kun, don't do that.

00:20:06.330 --> 00:20:08.420
Kaname-kun is sick...

00:20:08.420 --> 00:20:09.730
Huh? What?

00:20:16.200 --> 00:20:19.230
Hey. If you don't stop, you'll...

00:20:21.450 --> 00:20:24.410
So heavy. You're so heavy.

00:20:24.410 --> 00:20:25.840
I hit my chin.

00:20:25.840 --> 00:20:28.090
Shun's jump was too low.

00:20:28.090 --> 00:20:30.120
It wasn't my fault.

00:20:30.120 --> 00:20:32.120
You did this to yourselves.

00:20:47.820 --> 00:20:49.600
Sorry about today.

00:20:49.600 --> 00:20:51.400
We came to visit you,

00:20:51.400 --> 00:20:53.640
but all we did was make things worse.

00:20:54.360 --> 00:20:55.650
You really did.

00:20:57.450 --> 00:20:59.650
Take it easy tomorrow.

00:21:00.060 --> 00:21:02.900
You're taking tomorrow off, too?

00:21:03.400 --> 00:21:05.910
How does that negatively affect you?

00:21:06.390 --> 00:21:12.790
Actually, it'll be great going to 
school without you yelling at me.

00:21:13.020 --> 00:21:13.850
Huh?

00:21:16.180 --> 00:21:20.170
But it'll get boring without you, so get well soon.

00:21:22.090 --> 00:21:24.630
Take care, Kaname-kun.

00:21:24.630 --> 00:21:25.860
Bye bye.

00:21:29.310 --> 00:21:30.480
You heard them.

00:21:32.460 --> 00:21:34.490
Don't give me that.

00:21:34.790 --> 00:21:39.110
They shouldn't have made such a racket when they visited.

00:21:41.960 --> 00:21:45.450
But I think you're looking a little better.

00:21:46.760 --> 00:21:48.470
Your fever's down.

00:21:48.470 --> 00:21:50.270
All that racket made you sweat it out.

00:21:50.270 --> 00:21:51.450
Shut up.

00:21:55.770 --> 00:21:58.120
The rainy days continue.

00:21:58.890 --> 00:22:00.260
I hate the rainy season.

00:22:00.870 --> 00:22:03.420
I don't hate the rain, though.

00:22:04.370 --> 00:22:07.090
The rain pounds noisily on my window,

00:22:07.090 --> 00:22:10.000
but there's something comforting about the sound.

00:22:12.930 --> 00:22:13.970
Hisako,

00:22:15.290 --> 00:22:17.260
there are notebooks on my desk.

00:22:17.260 --> 00:22:18.170
Can you bring them to me?

00:22:18.170 --> 00:22:18.730
What?

00:22:19.270 --> 00:22:23.980
If I'm going to lie here, 
I might as well look over my notes.

00:22:24.290 --> 00:22:26.490
Actually,

00:22:27.220 --> 00:22:30.570
those boys just left with all of your notebooks.

00:22:30.570 --> 00:22:31.490
What?

00:22:34.720 --> 00:22:36.910
His notes are perfect.

00:22:36.910 --> 00:22:38.490
They really are.

00:22:39.240 --> 00:22:42.130
What did they come here for, exactly?!

00:24:16.680 --> 00:24:19.030
Next time: One Summer

00:24:16.680 --> 00:24:20.070
"One Summer"
